  "body": "There's no thread-mill tool kind.\n\n**Where:** `ToolKind` (`crates/tools/src/tools.rs:23`) has `Tap` and the lathe `Thread` insert, but no single-form or multi-form thread mill.\n\n**Effect:** thread milling is a common job on small CNC mills (interpolated threads in any material, large or odd sizes, no tap breakage). A vendor tool library can't carry thread mills at all. In one real catalog build, over 300 thread mills had to be left out.\n\n**Fix sketch:**\n- New kinds: single-form (one tooth, any pitch within range) and multi-form (several teeth, a fixed pitch). Each carries cutter diameter, form angle, pitch or pitch range, teeth count, neck and shank.\n- A thread-milling operation: helical interpolation, internal and external, climb or conventional, single or multi pass, radial passes.\n- Simulation and gouge laws for the form.\n\nEffort: max (a new kind, a helical op and the sim).\n\n**Done means:** a thread mill can be stored and used by a thread-milling op that verifies clean and posts helical G2/G3 with Z; pinned with goldens.\n",
